cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this data or code, please cite it as below."
title: "Detection is not resistance: frontier prompt-injection receipts"
authors:
  - family-names: Moon
    given-names: Bentley
type: dataset
license: MIT
keywords:
  - AI safety
  - prompt injection
  - LLM evaluation
  - oversight
abstract: >
  Preregistered Batch-API tests of prompt-injection resistance across three frontier
  models (Claude Opus 4.8, Sonnet 5, Haiku 4.5). Sonnet 5 detects 100% of a blatant
  injection while obeying 80% of it: detection is not resistance. A follow-up isolates
  the mechanism as channel/authority deference and shows a block-labeling defense that
  drives compliance to zero. Raw completions + a stdlib re-derivation script included.
